  "description": "timing.v1 §2.6: one reader's samples of one member, in arrival order, within one reading -> each sample's lifespan judgement. resource is {kind, annotations}, read as declarations.json reads one. epsilon_ms is the deployment's stated bound ε in milliseconds, null when none is stated. owners lists the meta.zid of each instance of the provider's address the reader holds a descriptor of, as written; one that is not 1 to 32 hexadecimal digits states none. A sample's stamp is null when it carries none, else {age_ms, id}: age_ms the reader's wall clock at the arrival minus the stamp's time, in milliseconds, exact to the nanosecond, negative when the stamp is ahead; id the stamp's id. Ids and zids compare by value, case and leading zeros ignored (core §3.3). Each expect entry is {verdict, reason}, by the first of these that holds: the resource is not a stream: not_this_profiles, kind; the declaration is invalid: unobservable, invalid; no timing.lifespan_ms: not_asked, no_lifespan; epsilon_ms null: unobservable, no_bound; no stamp: unobservable, unstamped; no owner's zid: unobservable, unattributed; the id is none of the owners': unobservable, foreign_stamp; the id's clock disagrees, because this stamp's age is below -ε, or an earlier sample of this case with the same id (by value) reached this step with an age below -ε: unobservable, clock_disagrees; age - ε above the lifespan: expired, expired; otherwise live, live. Both bounds are inclusive: an age of exactly the lifespan plus ε, or of exactly -ε, is live."
}
